---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const post = {
 title: 'NFPA 70E Embroidery Guide: Questions to Ask Before Decorating FR Shirts',
 description:
 'An educational guide to employer selection, garment labels, thread, backing, placement, and manufacturer approval for decorated arc-rated apparel.',
 category: 'NFPA 70E',
 readTime: '9 min read',
 date: 'May 9, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-05-09',
 image: '/images/generated/service-embroidery.jpg',
 slug: 'nfpa-70e-embroidery-guide',
}

const faqs = [
 { q: 'Can you embroider an arc-rated garment?', a: 'Only after the employer and garment manufacturer approve the exact thread, backing, method, size, and placement. Approval is product specific.' },
 { q: 'Does aramid thread make embroidery NFPA 70E compliant?', a: 'No. A thread label does not certify the finished garment. The complete decoration and garment require employer and manufacturer review.' },
 { q: 'Where can a logo go on an FR shirt?', a: 'Do not use a universal placement rule. Follow the exact manufacturer instructions or obtain written approval for the proposed garment, materials, size, and location.' },
 { q: 'Can screen printing be used instead?', a: 'It depends on the exact garment, ink, curing process, size, and placement. Obtain manufacturer and employer approval before production.' },
 { q: 'Can Bighorn select the required arc rating?', a: 'No. The employer selects protection from its electrical hazard and risk assessment. Bighorn can quote employer-selected products and coordinate documentation requests.' },
]

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
  {
   '@type': 'Article', headline: post.title, description: post.description,
   image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`, datePublished: post.isoDate,
   dateModified: '2026-08-21',
   author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
   publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' } },
   mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/${post.slug}/`,
   about: { '@type': 'Thing', name: 'NFPA 70E arc-rated apparel decoration review' },
  },
  {
   '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
   itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Safety and Compliance', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/${post.slug}/` },
   ],
  },
  { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: faq.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.a } })) },
 ],
}
---

<BaseLayout title={post.title} description={post.description} canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/${post.slug}/`} ogImage={post.image} type="article" publishedDate={post.isoDate}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
 <article class="bg-concrete">
  <header class="border-b border-hairline bg-navy-950 text-white">
   <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-20 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 lg:px-8">
    <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-navy-200" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
     <a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-400">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/safety-compliance/" class="hover:text-gold-400">Safety &amp; Compliance</a>
    </nav>
    <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-400">{post.category}</span>
    <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-navy-100">How to document a proposed decoration before it is added to employer-selected arc-rated apparel.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-navy-700 pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-navy-200">
     <span class="text-gold-400">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time>
    </div>
   </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <img src={post.image} alt="Embroidery sample prepared for review on an employer-selected garment" width="1200" height="675" loading="eager" class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover" />
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
    <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">Quick Answer</p>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl">Decoration can change an arc-rated garment. Document the exact product, thread, backing, method, size, and placement. Obtain written employer and manufacturer approval before production.</p>
   </aside>

   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">This article is educational. It does not perform an electrical hazard assessment, select PPE, or certify a finished garment.</p>

   <h2 id="roles" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Know Who Decides What</h2>
   <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <li><strong>The employer and safety lead</strong> assess the hazard and select the required protective system.</li>
    <li><strong>The garment manufacturer</strong> supplies the product label, arc rating, care instructions, and modification guidance.</li>
    <li><strong>The decorator</strong> documents the proposed materials, equipment, method, proof, and production controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Bighorn</strong> can coordinate a quote and request available documents from selected partners.</li>
   </ul>

   <h2 id="standard" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Use Current Standards and Product Documents</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><a href="https://www.nfpa.org/codes-and-standards/nfpa-70e-standard-development/70e" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">NFPA 70E</a> addresses electrical safety in the workplace. The employer should use the current edition and applicable OSHA requirements for its program.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A product label and manufacturer documents identify the exact garment. Do not infer an arc rating from fabric name, brand, color, or a general FR description.</p>

   <h2 id="decoration-inputs" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Document Every Decoration Input</h2>
   <ol class="mb-8 ml-6 list-decimal space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <li><strong>Garment.</strong> Manufacturer, model, size range, color, label, rating, and care instructions.</li>
    <li><strong>Thread.</strong> Brand, product, fiber, colors, and available technical data.</li>
    <li><strong>Backing and topping.</strong> Exact materials and whether they remain in the garment.</li>
    <li><strong>Method.</strong> Needle process, stitch file, density, finished dimensions, and placement.</li>
    <li><strong>Proof.</strong> Scaled artwork tied to the exact garment and size range.</li>
    <li><strong>Approval.</strong> Written acceptance from the employer and garment manufacturer.</li>
   </ol>

   <h2 id="thread" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Thread Alone Does Not Approve the Garment</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Aramid and other specialty threads may be available. That does not establish that the complete embroidery is suitable for a specific garment or hazard.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Ask the manufacturer to review thread, backing, stitch density, logo size, and placement together. Keep the response with the order record.</p>

   <h2 id="placement" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Placement Is Product Specific</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Do not use a universal chest, sleeve, or back rule. A manufacturer may limit decoration by area, layer, seam, pocket, label, or garment design.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Review every size in the program. A placement that fits one size may cross a seam, pocket, or label on another.</p>

   <h2 id="printing" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Screen Printing Needs the Same Review</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Printing adds ink, covered area, and a curing process. Supply the exact ink system, curing conditions, size, and placement to the garment manufacturer.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Do not describe a finished item as compliant based only on the ink or thread supplier's claim. The employer evaluates the complete protective system.</p>

   <h2 id="quote" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Build a Reviewable Quote</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A proposal should identify the exact garment, decoration materials, proof, quantities, sizes, pricing, expected timing, and approval dependencies. Availability and documentation depend on the selected manufacturer and production partner.</p>

   <section class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-panel p-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal">Need an arc-rated apparel proposal?</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-ash">Send the employer-selected garment, product documents, logo, placements, sizes, and quantities. We will coordinate a written proposal for review.</p>
    <a href="/get-a-quote/" class="btn-primary text-base">Get a Quote</a>
   </section>

   <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
     {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <div class="border border-hairline bg-paper p-6">
       <h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-charcoal">{faq.q}</h3>
       <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ash">{faq.a}</p>
      </div>
     ))}
    </div>
   </section>
  </div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
